                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a5cb542c-2be1-3835-ad7f-50e5ba0e7d39",
                        "entry_id": "8fa38806-4864-3d00-a6e2-aaaacf4fd372",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Hydrophilic."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "698f45fe-5e43-45c4-a095-ae0367f5c9fa",
                                "sense_id": "a5cb542c-2be1-3835-ad7f-50e5ba0e7d39",
                                "text": "lt is difficult to produce an absolutely non-irritant vaseline. Lanolin (wool fat) is indeed clear and smooth but it is neither very hydrophile nor neutral, so that it cannot be mixed with basic substances such as zinc oxide without saponifying."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "79154e8b-8abe-4dc3-b073-b8eff25d4909",
                                "sense_id": "a5cb542c-2be1-3835-ad7f-50e5ba0e7d39",
                                "text": "Partial dehydration of MetHb (by forming films at high relative humidities from solutions) produces a haemichrome structure of this molecule. These structural changes are prevented by binding the molecules to a very hydrophile dialdehyde - Sephadex carrier (DAS)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "90459895-7996-4295-ac0c-084b1399eb2d",
                                "sense_id": "a5cb542c-2be1-3835-ad7f-50e5ba0e7d39",
                                "text": "They are very hydrophile, and hydration of the particles is a factor sufficient to make the colloidal system stable even in the absence of stabilizing electrolytes, i.e. when the particles have no electrical charge of their own."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "305ae697-b6eb-48af-b4e5-17ed6d2d4788",
                                "sense_id": "a5cb542c-2be1-3835-ad7f-50e5ba0e7d39",
                                "text": "[...] reacts with water to a minimum extent, by contrast with minerals of the smectite group, which are regarded as very hydrophile due to their labile, “mobile” structure."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
